// expect-compile-error x86
// expect-exit: 0
// stage1-only
// SysV marshalling is register-only for now: an extern function whose
// parameter would spill to the stack is rejected rather than silently
// mismatched with the C convention. AAPCS64's eight s-registers accept
// all seven arguments, so on arm64 the declaration must simply compile.
extern fn bad(a f32, b f32, c f32, d f32, e f32, f f32, g f32) f32;
fn main() int {
	return 0;
}
